## The actual gap found (not assumed — read the real code)

services/gateway/src/services/llm-telemetry-service.ts's startLLMCall()
emits `llm.call.started/completed/failed` OASIS events carrying
{vtid, service, stage, provider, model, latency_ms} — exactly "which LLM
served this run", already queryable via queryLLMTelemetry(). This is the
existing mechanism VTID-03820's own DeepSeek override already flows
through (callViaRouter -> runProviderCall -> startLLMCall).

But dev-autopilot-execute.ts's runExecutionSession() tagged EVERY such
call — self-healing-triggered executions too, not just VTID-03820's
on-ramp — with a SYNTHETIC per-execution id, `VTID-DA-${executionId.slice(0,8)}`
(confirmed at the callMessagesApi call site and the runWorkerTask
vtid_like field), never `autopilot_recommendations.activated_vtid` (the
REAL task vtid a human sees on the board/drawer, and the one
getEventsForVtid()/the Pipelines trace view actually filter by).
Result: this telemetry has been invisible on every dev-autopilot
execution's own task, for as long as this code has existed — not a defect
introduced by VTID-03820, but the exact synthetic-id trap VTID-03820's own
metadata plumbing made newly worth fixing (its DeepSeek override is only
observable if the telemetry carrying provider=deepseek is actually
visible where a human looks).

## Fix

dev-autopilot-execute.ts: the existing, UNCONDITIONAL findingMetaR query
(already fetches spec_snapshot for scanner-based lesson lookup — no new
round trip) now also selects `activated_vtid`. New `telemetryVtid` =
activated_vtid if present, else the synthetic id (never blank — a finding
missing activated_vtid, e.g. very old rows, still gets tagged with
something). Both LLM-invocation call sites (the direct callMessagesApi
path and the worker-queue runWorkerTask path's vtid_like field) now use
telemetryVtid instead of the always-synthetic id.

No new UI, no new backend route, no new table/column — the fix is purely
"tag the existing telemetry event with the vtid the existing UI already
filters by." Provider/model already show 'deepseek'/'deepseek-flash' for
on-ramp-triggered calls (set by VTID-03820's override) vs. the self-healing
pipeline's own bedrock/anthropic values — no separate on-ramp flag needed,
the existing fields already distinguish them once actually visible.

